From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-11
Subject: [PATCH jm-v9 021] panfrost: add the Mali-G78 and G78AE model rows, match v9 ids by product biblioklept

Purpose: Let G78 and G78AE devices pass pan_get_model() and keep v9 parts
with an unexpected arch minor from being dropped as INCOMPATIBLE_DRIVER.
kbase names v9 products by arch major and product major only (mask
0xf00f): 0x9000 G77, 0x9001/0x9003 G57, 0x9002 G78, 0x9004 G68 and
0x9005 G78AE. Mesa keys on arch minor too, and parts differ there
(gs101's G78 reports 0x9202, upstream's G68 row is (9, 2, 4)). Add the
G78 row at (9, 2, 2) and G78AE at (9, 0, 5), and when no exact row
exists for an arch 9 id, match on arch major and product major.
G77 (9, 0, 0) from 006 is unchanged and agrees with malisx2 (0x9000) and
gs101 (PAN_PROD_ID(9, 0, 0)). G68 is upstream !43414, already in our base.
All v9 rows use the G57 16 KiB colour / 8 KiB depth tile buffer, as
malisx2 does for every arch 9 part. Transaction elimination produces
stale tiles on G78 (gs101 finding); panvk enables CRC only on v10+
(panvk_image.c), so no quirk is needed on v9.
Source/Reference: bmdhacks/malisx2 src/vk/mali_physical_device.c (MIT, id
table); Mesa bifrost cmdline.c GPU list; m8l8th814n-eng/mesa-gs101 0001/0003
(no licence: facts only, no code)
Tested GPU: build-checked (universal Android build v6-v14); not run on a G77/G78/G68/G78AE
Tested Kbase UAPI: none (table lookup only)
Mesa base range: 5a07217f + g615-v11-csf series + jm-v9 001-020
Dependencies: jm-v9 006
Validation test: vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices on a G78/G78AE (pending)

---
 src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c b/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c
index 82c4dc7..d386f74 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/model/pan_model.c
@@ -93,6 +93,14 @@ const struct pan_model pan_model_list[] = {
                                               MODEL_RATES_X(2, 4, 8,  32,  32, 8)),
    VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(9, 2, 4), 0, "G68",    "G78", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(16384,  8192),
                                               MODEL_RATES_X(2, 4, 8,  32,  32, 8)),
+   /* G78 (kbase TBEX, product major 2; Tensor gs101 reports 0x9202) and
+    * G78AE (product major 5): same v9 core and 16 KiB colour tile buffer as
+    * the G57/G68. Transaction elimination produces stale tiles on G78
+    * (gs101); panvk only enables CRC on v10+, so it stays off here. */
+   VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(9, 2, 2), 0, "G78",    "G78", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(16384,  8192),
+                                              MODEL_RATES_X(2, 4, 8,  32,  32, 8)),
+   VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(9, 0, 5), 0, "G78AE",  "G78", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(16384,  8192),
+                                              MODEL_RATES_X(2, 4, 8,  32,  32, 8)),
    /* G710 (kbase TODX, 0xa862): same Valhall v10 core as G610, 7-16 cores. */
    VALHALL_MODEL(PAN_PROD_ID(10, 8, 2), 0, "G710",   "G710", MODEL_ANISO(ALL),  MODEL_TB_SIZES(32768, 16384),
                                               MODEL_RATES_X(4, 8, 16,  64,  64, 16)),
@@ -160,5 +168,17 @@ pan_get_model(uint64_t gpu_id, uint32_t gpu_variant)
          return &pan_model_list[i];
    }
 
+   /* kbase names v9 products by arch major and product major only
+    * (GPU_ID2_PRODUCT_MODEL, mask 0xf00f): arch minor is not part of the
+    * product, and parts report different values (gs101's G78: 0x9202). */
+   if ((gpu_prod_id >> 16) == 9) {
+      for (unsigned i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(pan_model_list); ++i) {
+         if ((pan_model_list[i].gpu_prod_id & ~0xff00) ==
+                (gpu_prod_id & ~0xff00) &&
+             pan_model_list[i].gpu_variant == gpu_variant)
+            return &pan_model_list[i];
+      }
+   }
+
    return NULL;
 }
